  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-09T14:21:34.262Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When AddDamage action is used for players (i.e. not objects), target player is \"triggering player\".\nBut current implementation AddDamage also affects other players if broadcast type is not Local.\n\nNote:\n* Referenced from AddDamage document: \"To apply damage to the triggering player, leave receiver empty.\"  (https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/adddamage)\n* AddHealth has same rule (\"To apply health to the triggering player\"). So it might also have same issue. But I don't test it.\n\nTested environment: \n* Client: w_2019.2.3p1 build 793\n* SDK: VRCSDK-2019.06.04.14.12_Public\n\nReproduce world:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_6f13349b-79ce-4644-9f58-4ff4f0eec3d4\n\n\nLog:\n(trigger: OnInteract, broadcast type:AlwaysUnbuffered)\n\nTriggering player side / player: (naqtn 4ea2, w: 2)\n\n2019.06.09 22:02:10 Log        -  [VRC_TriggerInternal] 368.0483 AddDamageSwitch_AlwaysUnbuffered via Unnamed:OnInteract executing AddDamage\n2019.06.09 22:02:10 Log        -  [VRC_EventDispatcherRFC] Executing AddDamage on VRCPlayer[Local] naqtn 4ea2 2 (UnityEngine.GameObject) from Dispatcher (UnityEngine.GameObject) for naqtn 4ea2: S: \"\" I: 0 F: 200 B: False\n2019.06.09 22:02:10 Log        -  Local Death\n\n\nInvolved player side / player: (naqtn, w: 1)\n\n2019.06.09 22:02:10 Log        -  [VRC_EventLog] Deferring event [AddDamage/AlwaysUnbuffered w: 2 s:  i: 0 f: 200 b: False B: 0 p: ] because Instigator was not Local.\n2019.06.09 22:02:10 Log        -  [VRC_EventDispatcherRFC] Executing AddDamage on VRCPlayer[Local] naqtn 1 (UnityEngine.GameObject) from Dispatcher (UnityEngine.GameObject) for naqtn 4ea2: S: \"\" I: 0 F: 200 B: False\n2019.06.09 22:02:10 Log        -  Local Death",
  "error": null,
